    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Describing clothes and colours",
     "texto": [
      "Clothes usually take en or et: en jakke («a jacket»), et skjerf («a scarf»). Colours are adjectives that agree with the noun: en grønn jakke, et grønt skjerf.",
      "Many adjectives add -t with neuter nouns and -e in the plural: grønn, grønt, grønne. Unlike English adjectives, which never change, Norwegian adjectives agree with the gender and number of the noun."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Noun",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Adjective",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
